rnd_seed_low                                 = &BC      \ step 2 (decision 17): random's 16-bit state, the
rnd_seed_high                                = &BD      \ filing system's scratch (BUGS #12: not &92/&93)
\ BUGS #12: the generator was at &92/&93 until 2026-10-18, but the original's own
\ set_dying_mover_type_and_frame keeps a slot in &92 (STY &92 ... LDY &92), so every death set its
\ low byte. &BC/&BD: no write, read or execute by anything but random from start_game to the
\ title's give_irq_back (tools/zpwatch.mjs, jsbeeb 2.5.0, 2026-10-18: the front end's two games,
\ seeds 1, 3 and 5, both helicopter flights, the whole world to the completion text); the MOS and
\ DFS write them only while booting. They need last only from the seeding (take_irq_for_play,
\ just before its JMP start_game) to the game's end.
